cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AUTHBC — co-optimizing encoding, authentication placement, signature scheme and batching for UAV telemetry ledgers"
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Farouk
    given-names: Mohamed A.
repository-code: "https://github.com/besco1998/fanet-authbc"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible testbed for authenticated, blockchain-grade UAV telemetry ledgers over 802.11 FANET
  links, with a low-rate (LoRa) generalisation. Co-optimizes record encoding, authentication
  placement, signature scheme and batch size under joint constraints on verifiability, freshness
  and channel capacity. All results are derived from frozen, seeded data and re-checked on every
  run by an automated staleness gate.
keywords:
  - FANET
  - UAV telemetry
  - broadcast authentication
  - digital signatures
  - IEEE 802.11 DCF
  - LoRaWAN
  - reproducible research
license-url: "https://github.com/besco1998/fanet-authbc/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-07-30"
